<p>South Africa’s Constitutional Court on Friday set aside a December 2022 National Assembly vote that blocked impeachment proceedings against President Cyril Ramaphosa over the Phala Phala farm case, ruling that Parliament acted unlawfully and irrationally in halting the process. The court ordered lawmakers to resume scrutiny of an independent panel report and send the matter to an impeachment committee. The case centers on the 2020 theft of foreign currency from Ramaphosa’s Phala Phala game farm in Limpopo and allegations that he concealed the break-in from police and tax authorities. The scandal became a major political issue after a former intelligence official filed a complaint in 2022 accusing the president of handling the matter outside legal channels. Before the 2022 vote, an independent panel led by a retired judge found evidence warranting further investigation; the court case challenged Parliament’s decision not to move that report to the next stage.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/yKqNGyKh58aI8oebXKr0lJ8rIa3XiIJzUAOzqz4E0yy3xmlb_h3alzwmkfz0S5ORjXHQhhgfu3mauUlktl3OXeJEuVjXr2I1e6U0cCzBtVgB-Ul7k894PB4pS6fumYd7louCefIRiwNM4ye8YCmIU-oNSJp4xknzpiRiETfVolQaJ1uQqHBALa6c8T2qTACcvkK_qb0xWwyXUf59k-9GEUGAns0' alt='At the Constitutional Court in Johannesburg on Friday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Inquiry process: A committee formed under National Assembly Rule 129I can gather evidence, test claims and recommend whether Section 89 grounds exist for removal.</li><li>Political setting: News24 reported that parties in South Africa’s government of national unity face pressure over how they will handle the revived impeachment process.</li><li>Historic scale: Semafor said the majority ruling marks the first time in post-apartheid South Africa that a sitting president must face a formal inquiry of this scale.</li></ul><blockquote>President Cyril Ramaphosa respects the Constitutional Court’s judgment and reaffirms his commitment to the Constitution, the independence of the judiciary, and the rule of law. - The Presidency</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>The Presidency: The Presidency said Ramaphosa had consistently assisted inquiries into the matter and that allegations should be tested through the proper constitutional process. (<a href='https://thebulrushes.com/2026/05/08/phala-phala-concourt-rules-parliament-must-begin-impeachment-inquiry/'>The Bulrushes</a>)</li><li>Economic Freedom Fighters: EFF leader Julius Malema welcomed the ruling and said Ramaphosa must resign after the court set aside the National Assembly vote. (<a href='https://www.enca.com/news-top-stories-videos/malema-says-ramaphosa-must-resign-phala-phala-impeachment-revived'>eNCA</a>)</li><li>Standard Bank: Standard Bank CEO Sim Tshabalala said before the ruling that South Africa’s weak growth is rooted in the state’s inability to uphold the rule of law. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/08/2026/south-africas-top-court-revives-ramaphosa-impeachment-probe'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/8/south-africas-top-court-revives-impeachment-inquiry-against-president'>South Africa’s top court revives impeachment inquiry against president</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/08/2026/south-africas-top-court-revives-ramaphosa-impeachment-probe'>South Africa’s top court revives Ramaphosa impeachment probe</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.youtube.com/watch'>South Africa’s highest court revives impeachment proceedings against the president Cyril Ramaphosa</a> - youtube.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/08/world/africa/south-africa-president-ramaphosa-court-ruling-impeachment.html'>Court Revives ‘Farmgate’ Case Against South African President</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='http://www.africanews.com/2026/05/08/south-africa-top-court-revives-impeachment-inquiry-against-ramaphosa/'>South Africa top court revives impeachm